+    <help><![CDATA[
+This tool generates a Vitessce view configuration file (JSON) for visualizing single cell and spatial omics data in Galaxy.
+
+It combines processed AnnData, image data, and their metadata, produced by upstream WebAtlas tools, into a unified configuration that can be opened directly in the Vitessce viewer.
+
+----
+
+**Inputs**
+
+- **AnnData Zarr**
+  generated by *WebAtlas Process Files*
+
+- **Label image Zarr** *(optional)*
+  generated by *WebAtlas Consolidate Metadata*
+
+- **Label metadata JSON** *(optional)*
+  generated by *WebAtlas OME Zarr Metadata*
+
+- **Raw image Zarr** *(optional)*
+  generated by *WebAtlas Consolidate Metadata*
+
+- **Raw metadata JSON** *(optional)*
+  generated by *WebAtlas OME Zarr Metadata*
+
+Label and raw image inputs are optional and can be provided independently.
+
+----
+
+**Layout Options**
+
+The layout determines which visualization panels are shown in Vitessce.
+
+- **Minimal**
+  Spatial view and layer controller.
+
+- **Simple**
+  Extends the minimal layout by adding feature list and observation sets panels.
+  Enables exploration of gene expression and grouping of observations.
+
+- **Advanced**
+  Includes spatial view, layer controller, scatter plot, observation sets,
+  feature list, and genomic profiles panels.
+
+Panels not supported by the provided data are automatically hidden.
+
+Alternatively, a custom layout can be defined. See below for details.
+
+----
+
+**Vitessce Options**
+
+- **Spatial coordinates**
+  Location of spatial coordinates in the AnnData (e.g. *obsm/spatial*)
+
+- **Embeddings mapping**
+  Configure embeddings (e.g. spatial, PCA, UMAP) for scatter plots.
+  Define which dimensions are used for the x- and y-axis for each embedding.
+
+- **Factors**
+  Observation annotations displayed when hovering over cells.
+
+- **Sets**
+  Group observations into sets (e.g. clusters or cell types).
+  Supports scored sets (e.g. *celltype:probability*).
+
+- **Matrix**
+  Expression matrix used for visualization (e.g. *X* in the AnnData).
+
+----
+
+**Custom Layout**
+
+A custom Vitessce layout can be defined, replacing the predefined layout.
+Layout determines which visualization panels are shown in Vitessce.
+
+Syntax:
+    - Possible panels (case sensitive!): spatial, layerController, scatterplot,
+      featureList, obsSets, genomicProfiles
+    - Use "|" for left-to-right layout
+    - Use "/" for top-to-bottom layout
+    - Use parentheses for grouping
+
+Example inputs:
+    - spatial|layerController
+    - spatial|(layerController/(featureList|obsSets))
+    - layerController|spatial|((scatterplot/obsSets)|featureList)
+
+Notes:
+    - If a custom layout is provided, it overrides the predefined layout option.
+    - Panels not supported by the provided data (e.g. scatterplot without embeddings) are automatically hidden.
+    - Invalid panel identifiers are ignored or can lead to the tool failing.
+    - If the final expression is invalid, config generation may fail.
+
+----
+
+**Output**
+
+- **Vitessce configuration (JSON)**
+
+The output can be opened directly in Galaxy by clicking the **View** button in the history,
+which launches the integrated Vitessce visualization.
+    ]]></help>
+    <expand macro="citations"/>
+</tool>
