+    </tests>
+    <help><![CDATA[
+This tool generates a label TIFF image based on spatial metadata of the input data.
+
+For MERSCOPE data, it can additionally concatenate raw images into a single multichannel TIFF image.
+
+----
+
+**Supported Input Types**
+
+- **Visium AnnData (H5AD)**
+- **Visium SpaceRanger output archive (ZIP)**
+- **Xenium output archive (ZIP)**
+- **MERSCOPE output archive (ZIP)**
+
+----
+
+**Functionality**
+
+Depending on the input type, label images are generated as follows:
+
+- **Visium**
+    If SpaceRanger is provided as input, it is first converted into an AnnData object.
+    The observations are then reindexed to ensure numerical values, which are required for label image generation.
+    A label image TIFF file is then generated, with spots based on the spatial coordinates of the AnnData object.
+    Each spot is assigned a unique identifier, for example, a cell ID.
+
+- **Xenium**
+    A label image is generated with labels based on cell segmentation polygons from the Xenium output.
+    These polygons are converted into pixel coordinates and applied to the output image, assigning a unique label (e.g. cell ID) to each cell.
+
+- **MERSCOPE**
+    A label image is generated based on boundary information stored in the MERSCOPE data. Optionally, multiple Z-indices of the MERSCOPE data can be processed.
+
+Additionally, this tool can concatenate raw TIFF images from MERSCOPE into a single multichannel TIFF image per Z-index.
+This process is performed independently of the label image generation.
+
+----
+
+**Reference Image**
+    A reference image is required to determine the dimensions of the output label image.
+    For Visium data, this is optional, as the shape can be derived from the AnnData.
+
+----
+
+**Input type specific parameters**
+
+- **Visium**
+    - Subset AnnData on an obs column: Allows filtering of observations based on a specified column in the *obs* table. Only observations matching the specified values are kept in the dataset.
+    - Sample ID: Specify a sample ID if the dataset contains multiple samples and you wish to visualize a specific one.
+    - Relative size: Optional numerical *obs* column name that holds a multiplier for the spot diameter. Only useful for data that has been processed to merge spots.
+
+- **Xenium**
+    - Pixel resolution: Pixel resolution used for converting Xenium spatial coordinates to pixel coordinates.
+
+- **MERSCOPE**
+    - Z index: Z index of the MERSCOPE data that should be processed.
+
+----
+
+**Output**
+
+- **Label image (TIFF)**
+- **Multichannel raw image (TIFF, MERSCOPE only)**
+
+The output is used as input for the downstream WebAtlas tools **WebAtlas Consolidate Metadata** and **WebAtlas Write**.
+    ]]></help>
+    <expand macro="citations"/>
+</tool>
