+    <help><![CDATA[
+This tool converts supported spatial omics data formats into an AnnData object and subsequently into the Zarr format.
+It is used to standardize spatial omics data formats, ensuring compatibility with downstream visualization.
+
+----
+
+**Supported Input Types**
+
+- **AnnData file (H5AD)**
+- **SpaceRanger output archive (ZIP)**
+- **Xenium output archive (ZIP)**
+- **MERSCOPE output archive (ZIP)**
+
+----
+
+**Processing Steps**
+
+Regardless of input type, the following steps are performed:
+
+- Conversion to AnnData (if input is not already AnnData)
+- Standardization of data types and structure
+- Optional preprocessing (e.g. subsetting, embeddings)
+- Conversion to Zarr format
+
+----
+
+**Parameters**
+
+- **Output Zarr column chunk size**
+    Defines how many variables (e.g. genes) are stored per chunk in the Zarr representation of the expression matrix.
+    A single chunk contains all observations (e.g. cells) and the specified amount of variables.
+    Smaller chunks can lead to more efficient data retrieval in downstream analysis and visualization when accessing a small number of variables.
+    Larger chunks may improve writing speed to the Zarr format and improve performance when accessing larger portions of the dataset at the same time.
+
+- **Compute embeddings**
+    If enabled, PCA and UMAP embeddings are computed from the AnnData object if they are not already present.
+    These embeddings are usually required for downstream visualization.
+
+- **Alternative var index**
+    Specifies an alternative column in the *var* table to be used as the primary feature index.
+    This allows the use of specific identifiers, such as gene names, when the default index does not contain the desired values.
+
+- **Batch processing and batch size**
+    Enables incremental processing of the AnnData into Zarr in batches defined by batch size.
+    This prevents loading the full dataset into memory at once, making it useful for large datasets.
+    This is a trade-off between memory usage and runtime. It does not change the structure of the final Zarr output.
+
+- **Subset AnnData on an obs column**
+    Allows filtering of observations based on a specified column in the *obs* table. Only observations matching the specified values are kept in the dataset.
+
+- **Subset AnnData on a var column**
+    Allows filtering of variables based on a specified column in the *var* table (e.g. gene_ids). Only variables matching the specified values (e.g. A1CF, MSN) are kept in the dataset.
+
+- **Consolidate metadata**
+    Whether the Zarr metadata is consolidated, which can improve read performance by reducing the amount of metadata files that need to be accessed.
+    Disabling this is usually only useful if specific metadata entries wish to be modified. Only disable this if you have a specific use in mind.
+
+----
+
+**Input type specific parameters**
+
+- **SpaceRanger**
+
+  - Include clustering files: Whether cluster files from the SpaceRanger data are included in the AnnData object.
+  - Include embeddings: Whether embeddings (e.g. PCA, UMAP) from the SpaceRanger data are included in the AnnData object.
+  - Use raw matrix count file: Loads the raw matrix count file instead of the filtered matrix file.
+
+- **Xenium**
+
+  - Convert spatial coordinates to pixel coordinates: Convert Xenium spatial coordinates to pixel coordinates using the specified pixel resolution.
+  - Pixel resolution: Pixel resolution used for converting Xenium spatial coordinates to pixel coordinates.
+
+- **MERSCOPE**
+
+  - Filter prefix: Prefix to filter out of the MERSCOPE data.
+
+----
+
+**Output**
+
+- **AnnData Zarr dataset**
+
+The output is used as input for the downstream WebAtlas tools **WebAtlas Build Vitessce Config** and **WebAtlas Write**.
+    ]]></help>
+    <expand macro="citations"/>
+</tool>
