+    </tests>
+    <help><![CDATA[
+This tool converts spatial omics data into a SpatialData object and exports it as a Zarr dataset.
+
+----
+
+**Inputs**
+
+- **AnnData** (H5AD or Zarr)
+- **Label image (TIFF)** *(optional)*
+- **Raw image (TIFF)** *(optional)*
+
+Image inputs can be provided independently or omitted entirely.
+
+----
+
+**Functionality**
+
+The tool constructs a SpatialData object from the provided inputs:
+
+- The AnnData object is stored as a **table element**
+- The label image is stored as a **labels element**
+- The raw image is stored as an **image element**
+
+To ensure compatibility with the SpatialData format, the observation index of the AnnData object is adjusted.
+A new integer-based index *webatlas_index* is introduced while preserving the original observation index as *original_obs_index*.
+
+The resulting SpatialData object is written to Zarr format.
+
+----
+
+**Output**
+
+- **SpatialData object (Zarr, ZIP-compressed)**
+
+----
+
+**Use Case**
+
+This SpatialData object enables unified storage and handling of different types of spatial omics data (e.g. AnnData, label images, raw images) in a single data structure.
+It can be used in other tools or workflows that support SpatialData in Zarr format.
+
+SpatialData objects are not utilized by the WebAtlas pipeline itself.
+    ]]></help>
+    <expand macro="citations"/>
+</tool>
